            <ArticleTitle>Single proximal anastomosis for multiple vein coronary artery bypasses in diseased ascending aorta.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>125-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Minimization of the manipulation of the diseased ascending aorta has been shown to be associated with a reduced risk of postoperative stroke during coronary artery bypass surgery. We describe in this paper a novel method in which a single proximal anastomosis has been performed in the same ostium on the ascending aorta for multiple coronary artery vein grafts.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
